/* FILE: js/data/townsfolk_text.js
TOWNSFOLK TALK TABLES: the text and setup tables for the named townsfolk, moved verbatim from original lines
  32863-33108 (build 5109cd5), in place right after TOWNS IN PIXELS (drawTown ends at original line 32862 (build 5109cd5)).
It holds the TOWNSFOLK banner, then first and last names, tempers and voice pitch, the trades (FOLK_OCC: work spot, day,
  look, loves and hates, request kinds), greetings by town standing, trade talk, stories, deeds, weather and month lines,
  request wording, request chains, the life arcs, and the small seeded per-person accessors.
Entry points: the tables FOLK_OCC, FOLK_TALK, FOLK_GREET and the rest, and fMe, fKin, fKinRel, fArc, fStory, fChain.
Globals it owns (all const or function): FOLK_FN_F, FOLK_FN_M, FOLK_FN_K, FOLK_LN, FOLK_PERS, FOLK_VOICE, FOLK_OCC,
  FOLK_TRADES, FOLK_GREET, FOLK_GREETA, FOLK_INTRO, FOLK_TALK, FOLK_STORY, FOLK_DEED, FOLK_WX, FOLK_MONTH, FOLK_REQ,
  FOLK_CHAIN, FOLK_DONE, FOLK_ARCS, FOLK_TALK2, FOLK_TALKP, FOLK_SELF, FOLK_PET, FOLK_FEAR, FOLK_HABIT, fMe, fKin, fKinRel,
  fArc, fStory, fChain.
Main globals it reads from elsewhere, all at runtime inside the accessors: mulberry32 (original line 1441 (build 5109cd5)),
  cores and coresNear (original lines 2473 and 2492 (build 5109cd5)), and the townsfolk model later in index.html:
  fst, folkSlots, fDefById, folkDef and FOLKS (original lines 33111-33127 (build 5109cd5)).
Read at runtime by the townsfolk code later in index.html (folkDef, fDeedLine, fTx, fGenReq, openTalk, talkChat;
  original lines 33118-33421 (build 5109cd5)); nothing reads these tables at load.
Load-time statements: the const tables (pure literals) and one loop, original line 33084 (build 5109cd5), which appends
  FOLK_TALK2's lines to FOLK_TALK once; it needs both tables above it in this file and must run exactly once.
*/
/* ============================================================ *
 *  TOWNSFOLK (w4 · PT1 W7: no hearts) — Stardew-lite. Every harbour keeps a few NAMED folk (hamlet 3 · town 5 · grand 7 × ETUNE.folkN, plus
 *  the tavern's barkeep & one or two regulars), seeded per port — the same people every visit, every session: a trade, a
 *  temper, what their trade asks after, a home, a look & a portrait, and a day of their own (morning · afternoon ·
 *  evening · night) walked along the town's lanes.
 *  Talk (E / the pad's interact) and the town holds still under an FF-style box: Chat · Their request · Ask for gossip ·
 *  Farewell. No friendship per person (PT1 — the owner's call): their stories, their own requests and their leads open
 *  with the TOWN's standing (folkStand — W8's hidden reputation), and a favour you take lands in 📜 Contracts.
 *  What they remember lives in FOLKS (saved as 'folk': only folk you've met or carried word to) — additive: an older
 *  save simply knows nobody yet. Your deeds reach the wharf through NEWS ('fnews').
 * ============================================================ */
